                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.uri" : [ {
                  "value" : "http://test1.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/496164",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.legislation.history" : [ {
                  "value" : "<p>Legislative History:</p><p>The Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016</p><p></p><p>Short Title - The Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016</p><p>Act Number / Year - Act No. 49 of 2016</p><p>India Code Act ID - 201649</p><p>Introduced In - Parliament Rajya Sabha </p><p>Presidential Assent Date - December 27, 2016</p><p>Official Gazette Publication - December 28, 2016</p><p>Enforcement Date - April 19, 2017 </p><p> Nodal Ministry - Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment (Department of Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities)</p><p></p><p>Precedent &amp; Statutory Rationale</p><p></p><p>1.\tFulfilling International Obligations under UNCRPD:</p><p>o\tEnacted to give full effect to the United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities (UNCRPD), which India signed and ratified in 2007. </p><p></p><p>2.\tExpansion of Recognized Disability Categories:</p><p></p><p>o\tExpanded the recognized categories of disabilities from 7 (under the 1995 Act) to 21 conditions (including speech/language disabilities, autism spectrum disorder, cerebral palsy, muscular dystrophy, acid attack victims, chronic neurological conditions like Parkinson&#39;s/Multiple Sclerosis, and blood disorders like Thalassemia, Sickle Cell Disease, and Haemophilia). </p><p></p><p>3.\tRights-Based Enforcement &amp; Increased Reservation Mandates:</p><p></p><p>o\tReplaced the welfare approach with a rights-based framework, increasing government job reservations for persons with benchmark disabilities from 3% to 4% and higher education institution allocations to 5%. It also introduced statutory rights to non-discrimination, accessibility, inclusive education, and severe penalties for offences against persons with disabilities. </p><p></p><p>Parliamentary Trajectory &amp; Enactment</p><p></p><p>•\tFormulation: Drafted and piloted by the Department of Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities (DEPwD) under the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment following extensive consultation with disability rights organizations. </p><p>•\tParliamentary Passage: Introduced in the Rajya Sabha on February 7, 2014; referred to the Parliamentary Standing Committee on Social Justice and Empowerment; debated and passed by the Rajya Sabha on December 14, 2016, and subsequently passed by the Lok Sabha on December 16, 2016. </p><p>•\tPresidential Assent: Received formal Presidential Assent on December 27, 2016, entering the statute book as Act No. 49 of 2016. </p><p>•\tEnforcement: Brought into active operational force across India on April 19, 2017 via Official Gazette notification, with the accompanying national statutory rules notified on June 15, 2017. </p><p>Source: India Code Official Repository (indiacode.nic.in) and Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment (Department of Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities) Official Records.</p><p></p><p></p><p></p>",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
